{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":42789,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"6d98aa7cb10441bd10ef75ea4ec0059279aa16adadb80c20b25c45f6dbc2fdda","packTokens":27963,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":143,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"sketches","tokens":27789,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":10,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"sketches"},"pointers":[],"system":"Three engineers independently listed behaviours for the same request. Find where they DISAGREE about what the system should do (not wording differences).\nFor each disagreement: id D-1.., the span, a short topic, and the readings: which sketch (1-3), which behaviour index (0-based) in that span, and a one-line summary. Cite at least two different sketches. Empty list if they agree.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"sketches\" kind=\"sketches\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"sketch\": 1,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"39-reporting\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Reports are generated on demand (not real-time streaming) for a staff-selected date range, with three fixed report types.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff selects a date range and views 'Orders per Day' report showing date, order count, and order value per day within range\",\n     \"1: Staff views 'Top Products' report showing product, quantity sold, and revenue, ordered by some ranking (e.g. revenue desc)\",\n     \"2: Staff views 'Revenue per Customer' report showing customer, number of orders, and revenue for the range\",\n     \"3: Report values are computed from order/invoice data, not stored as static snapshots\",\n     \"4: If revenue calculation rules are undefined, system uses a documented default (e.g. order value sum) until clarified\",\n     \"5: Only staff roles can access report screens/endpoints; customer users cannot\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"40-report-filters\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Start/end date are mandatory filters; other filters are optional future enhancements not built now.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: User provides start date and end date; report results restricted to orders/data within that inclusive range\",\n     \"1: If start date is after end date, system rejects the filter with a validation message\",\n     \"2: If no date range is provided, system either defaults to a standard range or prompts user to select one\",\n     \"3: UI does not yet expose customer/product/category filters (deferred)\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"41-report-export\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"CSV export reproduces the same aggregated rows visible in the on-screen report, not raw underlying order data.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: User clicks 'Download CSV' on a report and receives a CSV file containing the same rows/columns shown in that report for the selected date range\",\n     \"1: Only authorized (staff) users can trigger CSV download\",\n     \"2: If report has no data for the range, CSV download still succeeds but contains header row only (or empty state is shown instead of enabling download)\",\n     \"3: Column order/formatting left as open point; a consistent default will be used until clarified\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"42-audit-history\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed event is logged automatically when the corresponding action occurs, including actor, timestamp, and target entity.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each of the listed events (user invited, user deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed) writes an audit log entry when it occurs\",\n     \"1: Audit entry records who performed the action, what action, what entity, and when\",\n     \"2: Only admin (or authorized staff) can view the audit history screen\",\n     \"3: System continues to function if audit log write fails, but such failure should itself be recorded/alerted (not silently dropped) — open point on exact behaviour\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"43-notifications\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed event triggers exactly one email to the relevant recipient at the moment the event occurs.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: User invited → invitation email sent with link to accept\",\n     \"1: Password reset requested → reset email sent with link/token\",\n     \"2: Order confirmed → confirmation email sent to customer\",\n     \"3: Order amended → amendment email sent to customer\",\n     \"4: Order status changed to out for delivery → notification email sent to customer\",\n     \"5: Order cancelled/rejected (where applicable) → notification email sent to customer\",\n     \"6: If email send fails, order/user process still completes but failure is logged/flagged for retry\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"44-email-provider\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Integration details are unresolved; system is built with a pluggable/abstracted email sending mechanism pending provider confirmation.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System sends outbound emails through a single integration point (provider, auth, sender/reply-to address, templates to be confirmed later)\",\n     \"1: If provider details unknown at delivery time, system must still be able to send via a placeholder/configurable provider without code changes to call sites\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"45-erp-stock-integration\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Stock import is read-only, one-directional (ERP→portal), scheduled nightly via CSV file ingestion.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System reads a nightly CSV file and updates stock quantities for matching products\",\n     \"1: Imported stock quantities are then reflected in catalogue/product stock displays\",\n     \"2: System never writes stock data back to the ERP\",\n     \"3: System never performs inventory transactions in the ERP\",\n     \"4: Import run outcome (success/failure, counts) is recorded, pending exact format clarification\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"46-data-retention\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Order/invoice records are never hard-deleted for 7 years; deleting a user only deactivates/removes their login access, not their historical order/invoice associations.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Order and invoice records remain stored and queryable for at least 7 years from creation\",\n     \"1: Users with appropriate permissions can view historical orders/invoices beyond normal operational windows\",\n     \"2: Deleting/deactivating a user does not delete or orphan that user's historical order or invoice records\",\n     \"3: Access to historical records is still governed by the viewer's role/customer-isolation rules\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"47-responsive-design\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All customer and staff pages must render and function correctly at phone, tablet, and desktop breakpoints, with buyer flows prioritized for mobile usability.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All pages are usable (readable, operable) on phone-sized viewports\",\n     \"1: All pages adapt to tablet and desktop viewports\",\n     \"2: Buyer-facing flows (catalogue, basket, checkout) are optimized primarily for mobile use\",\n     \"3: Exact supported browser/device matrix left open, default to common modern browsers until specified\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"48-performance\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"System must handle the stated scale (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day) with acceptable responsiveness on key flows, though no numeric SLA is fixed yet.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day)\",\n     \"1: System does not degrade to unusable/error states under this expected load\",\n     \"2: Specific response-time targets are undefined pending clarification\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"49-security\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Standard security controls are implemented as a baseline across the whole application, not just for one feature.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Users authenticate via secure login; passwords stored hashed (never plaintext)\",\n     \"1: Access to features/data is authorized based on user role (customer/staff/admin) and customer-level isolation\",\n     \"2: Sessions are managed securely (e.g. expiry, secure cookies)\",\n     \"3: Unauthorized API requests are rejected (401/403) rather than exposing data\",\n     \"4: Invalid or malicious input is rejected via validation, including file uploads\",\n     \"5: Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and unguessable\",\n     \"6: Production traffic is served only over HTTPS\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"50-data-isolation\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Customer-level isolation is enforced at the API/server layer for every endpoint returning customer-scoped data, not just hidden in the UI.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A customer user can only retrieve/view their own company's orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, and account info\",\n     \"1: Attempts to access another customer's data (e.g. via URL/ID manipulation) are rejected server-side with an authorization error, regardless of frontend state\",\n     \"2: All relevant API endpoints enforce ownership checks server-side, not relying on client-side filtering alone\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"51-accessibility\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Accessibility practices (keyboard nav, labels, contrast, screen-reader structure) are applied across the customer and staff portal UI as a general quality bar, no specific WCAG level fixed yet.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All interactive elements are reachable and operable via keyboard\",\n     \"1: Form fields have appropriate labels and accessible validation messages\",\n     \"2: Text/background contrast meets readable standards\",\n     \"3: Page structure supports screen readers (semantic markup, ARIA where needed)\",\n     \"4: Exact compliance target (e.g. WCAG AA) left open\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"52-error-handling\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Every listed failure scenario is caught and shown as a user-friendly message rather than a raw stack trace/server error.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Invalid login shows a clear 'incorrect credentials' style message, not a server error\",\n     \"1: Expired password-reset link shows a friendly expiry message with option to request a new one\",\n     \"2: Attempting to order/view a no-longer-available product shows a friendly unavailable message\",\n     \"3: Stock import failure is reported via friendly status, not raw exception\",\n     \"4: Failed order submission shows a retryable friendly error, order is not silently lost or duplicated\",\n     \"5: Email delivery failure does not break the triggering workflow and is not shown as a raw error to the end user\",\n     \"6: Invalid CSV upload shows friendly validation errors identifying the problem\",\n     \"7: Missing product (e.g. deep link to deleted product) shows a friendly not-found message\",\n     \"8: Session expiration redirects to sign-in with a friendly message rather than exposing an error page\",\n     \"9: No raw stack traces, SQL errors, or internal technical details are ever shown to end users\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"53-empty-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed scenario shows a distinct, friendly empty-state message/UI rather than a blank screen or generic error.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Search with no matches shows 'no results' message with guidance\",\n     \"1: Empty basket shows an empty-basket message with a call to action (e.g. browse catalogue)\",\n     \"2: No orders yet shows an appropriate empty message on 'my orders'/order queue\",\n     \"3: No invoices shows an appropriate empty message on invoice list\",\n     \"4: No saved basket templates shows an appropriate empty message\",\n     \"5: No matching products (e.g. category/filter with none) shows empty state\",\n     \"6: Report run with no results in range shows empty-state message instead of blank table\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"54-loading-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed async operation shows a visible loading indicator while in progress, and resolves to success/error/empty state afterward.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each show a loading indicator while data is being fetched/processed\",\n     \"1: If an operation takes unusually long or times out, the loading state resolves to an error state rather than hanging indefinitely\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 16 listed customer screens must exist as distinct, navigable pages in the delivered product.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer can navigate to and use: sign in, forgot password, reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list, invoice detail, saved basket templates, account/company details, delivery addresses\",\n     \"1: These screens are accessible only to authenticated customer users (except sign in/forgot/reset password which are pre-auth)\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 11 listed staff screens must exist and be accessible only to staff role.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff can navigate to and use: staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list, customer detail, customer orders, customer invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management\",\n     \"1: These screens require staff (or higher) authentication; customer users cannot access them\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 13 listed admin screens must exist and be restricted to admin role only.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Admin can navigate to and use: admin dashboard, users, user detail, customers, customer detail, products, product editor, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, price list editor, system/import status, audit history\",\n     \"1: These screens require admin-level authentication; staff and customer users cannot access them\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Order status transitions strictly follow the documented sequence; cancellation is only allowed from 'Received' state, and staff rejection/cancellation rules may add additional exits beyond customer-initiated ones.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Order progresses through statuses: Received → Confirmed → Picking → Out for Delivery → Delivered → Invoice Created\",\n     \"1: Order transitioning to Delivered automatically triggers invoice creation\",\n     \"2: Order can transition from Received directly to Cancelled (customer-initiated, before confirmation)\",\n     \"3: Order cannot be cancelled by customer once in Confirmed or later status\",\n     \"4: Staff can reject/cancel an order per business rules even outside the customer-cancel window (exact rules open)\",\n     \"5: Any attempted status transition outside the defined sequence is rejected\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Invoice is auto-created on delivery, starts as Unpaid, and can move to Paid (staff action) or Overdue (automatic based on rules TBD).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Invoice is created automatically when order status becomes Delivered\",\n     \"1: New invoice defaults to Unpaid status\",\n     \"2: Staff can mark an invoice as Paid\",\n     \"3: Invoice may transition to Overdue status automatically based on rules to be defined (e.g. a background job)\",\n     \"4: Invoice cannot be created for an order that has not reached Delivered status\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a conceptual data model list guiding what persisted records the system must support; not literal schema requirement, so behaviours focus on 'system stores/relates X'.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System persists and relates records for users, roles, customers, customer-users, addresses, products, categories, manufacturers, vehicles, product-vehicle compatibility, price lists/items, customer price lists, stock items/imports, baskets/items/templates, orders/items/status history, invoices/items, payments, audit logs, and email notifications\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed API area corresponds to actual callable endpoints backing the UI behaviours described elsewhere; listed as required backend capability, not new behaviour beyond what's described in other sections.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Backend exposes endpoints for authentication (sign in/out, password reset, invitation acceptance, session status), catalogue (list/detail/search/compatibility), basket (get/add/update/remove/clear), checkout (validate/delivery options/submit), orders (customer and staff list/detail/edit/confirm/reject/status/repeat/cancel/staff-created), invoices (list/detail/pdf/mark paid), administration (users/customers/products/categories/price lists/compatibility/imports/audit logs), and reports (3 report types + CSV export)\",\n     \"1: Each endpoint enforces role-appropriate authorization (customer vs staff vs admin)\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed task runs automatically on a schedule/trigger without manual staff action, producing observable side effects (stock updated, emails sent, invoices created, tokens cleaned).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Nightly job imports ERP stock CSV automatically\",\n     \"1: Email sending is processed by a background job/queue rather than blocking user requests\",\n     \"2: Invoice generation runs automatically upon order delivery (as a background process)\",\n     \"3: A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on rules\",\n     \"4: A scheduled job removes/expires old password-reset tokens so they can no longer be used\",\n     \"5: A scheduled job expires stale invitations so they can no longer be accepted\",\n     \"6: If a scheduled job fails, it does not silently retry forever or corrupt data; failure is logged (ties to audit/ERP import failure event)\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"System needs durable file storage for product images and invoice PDFs at minimum, with CSV/report storage as 'potential' (lower certainty) needs.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Product images are stored and retrievable for display in catalogue/product detail\",\n     \"1: Invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download\",\n     \"2: ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be stored, pending confirmation\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Portal generates an invoice PDF (format/branding TBD) and makes it downloadable; exact template fidelity is unresolved.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices\",\n     \"1: Staff can download/view PDF of any invoice within their access\",\n     \"2: If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download\",\n     \"3: Template branding, tax info, numbering scheme are open points pending clarification\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"65-csv-import-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The nightly ERP CSV import performs all listed validations before/while processing, rejecting invalid rows/files and reporting a structured result.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Import rejects/flags a file missing required headers\",\n     \"1: Import rejects/flags rows referencing unknown product codes, reporting them\",\n     \"2: Import rejects/flags rows with non-numeric quantities\",\n     \"3: Import rejects/flags invalid negative quantities (unless explicitly allowed)\",\n     \"4: Import detects and reports duplicate product identifiers within the file\",\n     \"5: Import rejects/flags an empty file\",\n     \"6: Each import run produces a result summary: records received, records processed successfully, records rejected, and error details\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"66-csv-export-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All CSV exports (reports etc.) across the system follow a consistent formatting standard and are access-controlled.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Exported CSVs include a header row with consistent column names\",\n     \"1: Dates/times in exports use a single consistent format across all exports\",\n     \"2: Numbers in exports use a single consistent format (e.g. decimal separator) across all exports\",\n     \"3: Only authorized users (per report/data access rules) can download export files\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"67-business-rules-summary\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints throughout the system (cross-cutting, restating/binding behaviours already described elsewhere).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer users only ever see their own company's data (orders, invoices, pricing, etc.)\",\n     \"1: Customer product pricing is derived from their assigned price list, not a global price\",\n     \"2: Stock quantities shown come only from the nightly ERP CSV import\",\n     \"3: No code path writes stock updates back to the ERP\",\n     \"4: Stock import happens nightly on a schedule\",\n     \"5: Earliest delivery date is computed based on 14:00 cutoff rule relative to order submission time\",\n     \"6: Customer can repeat a previous order to quickly recreate a basket\",\n     \"7: Customer can save and reuse named basket templates\",\n     \"8: Customer cancellation is blocked once order is Confirmed or later\",\n     \"9: Staff can edit order contents while order is pre-Confirmed\",\n     \"10: Customer receives notification email when order is confirmed\",\n     \"11: Customer receives notification email when order is out for delivery\",\n     \"12: Invoice is created automatically at Delivered status, not before\",\n     \"13: Staff can manually mark invoices as paid\",\n     \"14: Deactivating a user does not remove their historical order/invoice records\",\n     \"15: Order and invoice records are retained at least 7 years\",\n     \"16: No online payment capture functionality is built\",\n     \"17: No native mobile app is built\",\n     \"18: No delivery route planning functionality is built\",\n     \"19: No returns/credit-note functionality is built\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These items are explicitly excluded from phase 1 delivery; any related requests should be flagged as out of scope rather than implemented.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System does not implement online card payment processing\",\n     \"1: System does not provide a native iOS or Android application\",\n     \"2: System does not provide multi-language/localization support\",\n     \"3: System does not implement delivery route planning or driver route optimization\",\n     \"4: System does not implement returns management or credit notes\",\n     \"5: System does not write inventory data back to the ERP\",\n     \"6: System does not provide customer self-service returns\",\n     \"7: System does not provide marketplace functionality (e.g. multi-vendor)\",\n     \"8: System does not implement promotions, coupons, volume discounts, tiered or contract-specific pricing unless separately approved\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are unresolved requirements; no behaviour is specified until answered — flagged as assumptions/risks rather than implemented features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Numerous functional details (self-registration, password policy, MFA, SSO, lockout behaviour, address creation rules, category structure, product attributes/variants, vehicle data source, tax treatment, discounts, stock semantics, backordering, delivery slots/zones, invoice numbering/VAT, payment recording, email provider specifics, hosting/environments, audit retention, report revenue definition) remain undefined and must be resolved or assumed explicitly before implementation\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) must exist as part of delivery, with deployment pipeline between them.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Code can be run/deployed in local development, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments distinctly\",\n     \"1: Exact deployment/promotion strategy between environments is unresolved pending clarification\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Automated/manual test coverage must exist for each listed scenario across the listed functional areas before release.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Tests verify successful login, invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login attempts behave correctly\",\n     \"1: Tests verify customer isolation, staff access, admin access, and rejection of unauthorized API access\",\n     \"2: Tests verify catalogue listing, search, category filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired product handling, and product image display\",\n     \"3: Tests verify correct price list application, price change handling, preservation of price on existing orders, and pricing customer isolation\",\n     \"4: Tests verify valid/invalid stock imports, duplicate/unknown product handling, out-of-stock and low-stock behaviour\",\n     \"5: Tests verify basket add/remove/update, quantity validation, delivery-date rule computation, address selection, order submission, and duplicate submission prevention\",\n     \"6: Tests verify order creation, confirmation, staff editing, customer cancellation, reordering, status transitions, and triggered email notifications\",\n     \"7: Tests verify automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid\",\n     \"8: Tests verify report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are binding, literal acceptance tests to be implemented exactly as written (customer isolation, pricing snapshot, 14:00 cutoff, cancellation window, auto invoice creation).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer A requesting orders never receives Customer B's orders, even via direct ID/URL manipulation in API calls\",\n     \"1: Product price shown to Customer A reflects Price List A assigned to them\",\n     \"2: Orders retain the price at time of placement even if the customer's price list changes afterward\",\n     \"3: Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date\",\n     \"4: Order submitted at/after 14:00 on a working day gets the following working day as earliest delivery date\",\n     \"5: Customer cancelling a Received order moves it to Cancelled\",\n     \"6: Customer attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked\",\n     \"7: Order moving to Delivered status (successfully saved) automatically creates an invoice for that order\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"73-suggested-delivery-phases\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a planning/sequencing artifact, not a behavioural requirement in itself — no new system behaviour beyond what's described in other sections.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: No additional system behaviour beyond phased grouping of previously described features (foundation, catalogue, ordering, staff ops, invoicing, administration, integrations/reporting, QA/production)\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 2,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"39-reporting\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff (not customers) can access three required reports (Orders per Day, Top Products, Revenue per Customer) filtered by a selected date range.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff selects a date range and views Orders per Day report showing date, order count, and order value per day within range.\",\n     \"1: Staff views Top Products report showing product name, quantity sold, and revenue for the selected range.\",\n     \"2: Staff views Revenue per Customer report showing customer name, number of orders, and revenue for the selected range.\",\n     \"3: Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users cannot view reports.\",\n     \"4: If no orders exist in the range, each report shows zero/empty rows rather than erroring.\",\n     \"5: Report revenue calculation includes/excludes cancelled orders and tax per a defined rule (currently undefined, flagged as open point).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"40-report-filters\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Start/end date filters are mandatory for all reports; customer/product/category filters are optional/not required in phase 1.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: User enters start date and end date and report results update to only include records within that inclusive range.\",\n     \"1: If start date is after end date, system shows a validation error and does not run the report.\",\n     \"2: If no date range is supplied, system applies a default range or prompts the user (open point, default behaviour to be defined).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"41-report-export\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the three reports can be exported as CSV matching the on-screen data for the currently applied filters.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff clicks 'Export CSV' on a report and downloads a CSV file containing the same rows/columns shown on screen for the current filter.\",\n     \"1: CSV filename reflects report type and date range.\",\n     \"2: Only staff with report access can trigger export.\",\n     \"3: Exporting an empty report (no results) still produces a valid CSV with header row only.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"42-audit-history\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Every listed event type is recorded as an immutable audit log entry visible to authorized staff/admin.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System writes an audit log entry (actor, action type, target entity, timestamp) whenever any listed event occurs: user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed.\",\n     \"1: Only admin (and possibly staff) can view the Audit History screen; customers cannot.\",\n     \"2: Admin views audit history list, filterable/sortable by date, user, or action type.\",\n     \"3: If an audited action fails before completion, no audit log entry for success is written (only failure events like ERP import failed).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"43-notifications\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed event automatically triggers a system email to the relevant recipient via the configured email provider.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Inviting a user sends an invitation email with a link to set up the account.\",\n     \"1: Requesting password reset sends an email with a reset link.\",\n     \"2: Confirming an order sends an order confirmation email to the customer.\",\n     \"3: Amending an order sends an order amendment email to the customer.\",\n     \"4: Marking an order out for delivery sends a notification email to the customer.\",\n     \"5: Cancelling/rejecting an order sends a cancellation/rejection email where applicable.\",\n     \"6: If email sending fails, the triggering action (e.g. order confirmation) still completes and failure is logged rather than blocking the user.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"44-email-provider\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The application integrates with a yet-undetermined client email provider; concrete configuration is deferred.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Outgoing emails are sent using the client's configured provider credentials (SMTP or API) once determined.\",\n     \"1: Sender and reply-to addresses are configurable rather than hard-coded.\",\n     \"2: Provider/auth/template/bounce-handling specifics remain open and not yet implemented behaviours.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"45-erp-stock-integration\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A nightly scheduled job reads a CSV file supplied by the ERP, imports stock quantities into the portal, and never writes back to the ERP.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Scheduled nightly job reads the ERP CSV file and updates stock quantities for matched products.\",\n     \"1: Portal never writes stock changes or inventory transactions back to the ERP system.\",\n     \"2: If the file cannot be read/parsed, the import fails and an error/notification is generated (mechanism open).\",\n     \"3: Exact file delivery, format, product identifier, frequency, and retention of historical imports are open points not yet defined.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"46-data-retention\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Orders and invoices must be stored for at least 7 years and remain visible to users with appropriate permission even after the acting user is deleted.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Order and invoice records are retained in the system for a minimum of 7 years from creation.\",\n     \"1: Authorized users can still view historical orders/invoices tied to a deactivated/deleted user.\",\n     \"2: Deleting a user account does not delete or cascade-delete that user's associated order/invoice records.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"47-responsive-design\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All customer and staff pages must render and function correctly on mobile, tablet, and desktop, with mobile given priority for buyer screens.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Buyer-facing pages (catalogue, basket, checkout, etc.) are fully usable with touch input on small mobile screens.\",\n     \"1: Same pages adapt layout correctly on tablet and desktop viewports.\",\n     \"2: Exact supported browser/device matrix is undefined; no specific legacy browser support guaranteed.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"48-performance\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The system must handle expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day) with reasonable response times on key workflows, though no numeric targets are fixed.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under expected concurrent load.\",\n     \"1: No explicit SLA/response-time thresholds are defined yet (open point).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"49-security\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Standard web security controls are implemented application-wide: secure auth, hashed passwords, RBAC, tenant isolation, secure sessions, API protection, input/file validation, common-vulnerability protection, secure reset tokens, HTTPS in prod.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: User passwords are stored hashed (e.g. bcrypt), never in plaintext.\",\n     \"1: Each API endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side (customer/staff/admin).\",\n     \"2: Unauthenticated or unauthorized API requests are rejected with 401/403 responses.\",\n     \"3: File uploads are validated for type/size before acceptance; invalid files are rejected.\",\n     \"4: Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and cryptographically secure.\",\n     \"5: Production traffic is served only over HTTPS.\",\n     \"6: Input validation rejects malformed/malicious input (e.g. XSS, SQL injection attempts) with safe error responses.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"50-data-isolation\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Server-side authorization strictly prevents any customer user from accessing another customer's orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, or account info, regardless of frontend state.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer user requesting their own orders/invoices/addresses/pricing/users/account info receives only their own company's data.\",\n     \"1: Customer user attempting to access another customer's data (e.g. by changing an ID in the URL/API) receives a 403/404, not the data.\",\n     \"2: Authorization checks are enforced in backend API logic, not only hidden/disabled in the UI.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"51-accessibility\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The portal is designed following accessible practices (keyboard nav, labels, contrast, screen-reader structure) without committing to a specific WCAG conformance level.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All interactive elements are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\",\n     \"1: Form fields have associated labels and validation messages are announced/readable by screen readers.\",\n     \"2: Text and UI elements meet readable contrast levels.\",\n     \"3: Specific compliance target (e.g. WCAG 2.1 AA) is not fixed (open point).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"52-error-handling\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"User-facing errors across the listed scenarios show friendly messages, never raw stack traces or internal details.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Invalid login shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message, not which field was wrong.\",\n     \"1: Expired password-reset link shows a message prompting the user to request a new one.\",\n     \"2: Attempting to order a product no longer available shows a friendly 'no longer available' message.\",\n     \"3: Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all produce user-friendly messages without exposing stack traces/sensitive info.\",\n     \"4: Session expiration redirects user to sign-in with a message, preserving no sensitive cached data.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"53-empty-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed list/search view shows a dedicated empty-state message/UI when there is no data, rather than a blank screen.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Search with no matches shows 'no results' empty state with suggestion to adjust search.\",\n     \"1: Empty basket shows an empty-basket message with a call to browse catalogue.\",\n     \"2: No orders/invoices/templates/report results show respective friendly empty-state messaging instead of blank tables.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"54-loading-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed async operation/screen shows a visible loading indicator (spinner/skeleton) while data is fetched.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each display a loading indicator while processing, then replace it with results or an error.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 16 listed customer screens must exist as a distinct, navigable page in the portal.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer can navigate to and use each of: sign in, forgot password, reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list, invoice detail, saved basket templates, account/company details, delivery addresses.\",\n     \"1: Unauthenticated users can only access sign-in/forgot/reset password screens, not authenticated customer screens.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 11 listed staff screens must exist and be accessible only to staff/admin roles.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff can navigate to and use each of: staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list, customer detail, customer orders, customer invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management.\",\n     \"1: Customer users cannot access any staff screen URLs even directly.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 13 listed admin screens must exist and be restricted to admin role only.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Admin can navigate to and use each of: admin dashboard, users, user detail, customers, customer detail, products, product editor, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, price list editor, system/import status, audit history.\",\n     \"1: Staff (non-admin) and customer users are blocked from admin screens/routes.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Orders move through a fixed sequence of statuses (Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for Delivery→Delivered→Invoice Created), with cancellation only allowed pre-confirmation.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: New order is created with status Received, and progresses through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence as staff update status.\",\n     \"1: Delivered status triggers automatic invoice creation.\",\n     \"2: Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled.\",\n     \"3: Attempting to cancel an order once it is Confirmed or later is rejected by the system.\",\n     \"4: Staff-initiated rejection/cancellation at other stages follows separate business rules (not fully specified).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"An invoice is auto-created when an order is marked Delivered, starting as Unpaid, and can transition to Paid or Overdue.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Marking an order Delivered automatically creates an invoice with status Unpaid.\",\n     \"1: Staff can mark an invoice as Paid.\",\n     \"2: Invoice transitions to Overdue based on rules not yet defined (open point).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a conceptual data model list guiding implementation, not literal schema behaviours — no direct observable behaviour required.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System's underlying data model conceptually includes entities such as User, Role, Customer, Product, Order, Invoice, AuditLog, EmailNotification, etc., to support all described behaviours.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Backend exposes API endpoints grouped by these functional areas, each requiring appropriate auth/role enforcement.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Authentication APIs support sign in, sign out, password reset, invitation acceptance, and session/account status checks.\",\n     \"1: Catalogue APIs return products, categories, product details, search results, and vehicle compatibility data.\",\n     \"2: Basket APIs support get/add/update/remove/clear operations scoped to the authenticated customer's basket.\",\n     \"3: Checkout APIs validate basket contents, return delivery options, and submit orders.\",\n     \"4: Order APIs provide customer and staff order lists/detail, repeat order, cancel, staff edit/confirm/reject/status update, and staff-created orders.\",\n     \"5: Invoice APIs provide list, detail, PDF download, and mark-paid actions.\",\n     \"6: Administration APIs (users, customers, products, categories, price lists, vehicle compatibility, imports, audit logs) are restricted to admin role.\",\n     \"7: Report APIs return orders-per-day, top-products, revenue-by-customer data and CSV exports.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Scheduled/background jobs run automatically for the listed maintenance tasks without manual staff triggering.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Nightly job automatically imports ERP stock CSV without manual intervention.\",\n     \"1: Emails are sent asynchronously via a background job/queue rather than blocking the triggering request.\",\n     \"2: Invoice generation runs automatically as a background process when an order is delivered.\",\n     \"3: A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on defined rules.\",\n     \"4: Expired password-reset tokens and stale invitations are automatically cleaned up/expired by a scheduled job.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The system persists uploaded/generated files (product images, invoice PDFs, ERP CSVs, report files) in a durable storage location accessible to authorized features.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Uploaded product images are stored and retrievable for display on catalogue/product pages.\",\n     \"1: Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download.\",\n     \"2: ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be persisted (provider/location open point).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each created invoice has a corresponding PDF that customers and staff can download; exact template/branding specifics are open.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices from the invoice detail screen.\",\n     \"1: Staff can download/view invoice PDFs for any customer's invoice.\",\n     \"2: If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download, and can retry.\",\n     \"3: Template, branding, tax info, and numbering scheme are unresolved open points.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"65-csv-import-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The nightly ERP CSV import performs listed validations before applying stock changes, and reports results, rejecting invalid rows while continuing with valid ones.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Import validates required headers exist before processing; aborts with error if missing.\",\n     \"1: Rows with non-numeric quantities are rejected and reported, not applied.\",\n     \"2: Rows with invalid negative quantities are rejected unless explicitly supported.\",\n     \"3: Duplicate product identifiers within the file are detected and reported as errors.\",\n     \"4: Unknown product identifiers (not matching any portal product) are reported as errors, not silently ignored.\",\n     \"5: An empty file is rejected with an error rather than clearing all stock.\",\n     \"6: After each import, system records counts of records received, processed successfully, rejected, plus error details, accessible via System/Import status screen.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"66-csv-export-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All CSV exports across the system follow consistent formatting standards and are access-controlled.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Every CSV export includes a header row with consistent, human-readable column names.\",\n     \"1: Dates/times in exports use one consistent format; numbers use one consistent format (e.g. decimal separators) across all exports.\",\n     \"2: Only authorized users (role-appropriate) can trigger/download a given CSV export; unauthorized requests are rejected.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"67-business-rules-summary\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints system-wide unless later changed.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Customer users' data queries (orders, invoices, etc.) are always scoped to their own company only.\",\n     \"1: Product prices shown/applied to a customer are derived from that customer's assigned price list.\",\n     \"2: Stock values displayed come solely from the last successful ERP CSV import; portal never pushes stock changes to ERP.\",\n     \"3: Stock import runs nightly on schedule.\",\n     \"4: Earliest delivery date offered at checkout is computed from order submission time relative to 14:00 cutoff.\",\n     \"5: Customer can trigger 'repeat order' to recreate a basket from a past order.\",\n     \"6: Customer can save a named basket template and reuse it later.\",\n     \"7: Customer cancellation action is blocked once an order is Confirmed or later (enforced server-side).\",\n     \"8: Staff can modify order contents only while order is pre-confirmation.\",\n     \"9: Email notification fires automatically on order confirmation and on out-for-delivery status change.\",\n     \"10: Invoice is created automatically the moment an order's status becomes Delivered.\",\n     \"11: Staff can manually mark any invoice as Paid.\",\n     \"12: Deactivating a user does not remove their historical orders/invoices from reports or records.\",\n     \"13: Order/invoice records persist in the system for at least 7 years.\",\n     \"14: No online payment capture features are present; payment status must be set manually by staff.\",\n     \"15: No native mobile app, delivery route planning, returns, or credit note functionality is present in this phase.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The listed features are explicitly not built in phase 1; any UI referencing them is absent.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: No card payment flow, native app, multi-language switch, route planning, returns/credit-note screens, ERP write-back, or promotional/coupon/tiered-pricing features exist in the delivered system unless separately approved.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These remain unresolved; no committed behaviour yet — flagged for clarification rather than implemented.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: No behaviour is implemented for items still under open question (self-registration, MFA, SSO, lockout policy, variants, substitutes, compatibility data source, volume/promo pricing, backordering, partial fulfillment, delivery slots/zones, VAT, credit notes, payment import, bounce tracking, hosting/provider choice, pen-testing, IP restriction) until clarified.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) are provisioned for the project lifecycle.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Code can be deployed and run independently in local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments with environment-specific configuration.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Automated/manual test coverage exists for each listed scenario across auth, authorization, catalogue, pricing, stock, basket/checkout, orders, invoices, and reporting.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Test suite verifies successful and invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login rejection.\",\n     \"1: Test suite verifies customer data isolation, staff/admin access boundaries, and rejection of unauthorized API calls.\",\n     \"2: Test suite verifies catalogue listing/search/filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired-product exclusion, and image display.\",\n     \"3: Test suite verifies correct price-list pricing, price change handling, and that historical orders retain original price.\",\n     \"4: Test suite verifies valid/invalid/duplicate/unknown-product stock imports and out-of-stock/low-stock status display.\",\n     \"5: Test suite verifies basket operations, quantity validation, delivery-date rule, address selection, order submission, and duplicate-submission prevention.\",\n     \"6: Test suite verifies order creation, confirmation, staff editing, cancellation, reorder, status transitions, and triggered email notifications.\",\n     \"7: Test suite verifies automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid.\",\n     \"8: Test suite verifies report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These given/when/then examples are binding acceptance tests for isolation, pricing, delivery date, cancellation, and invoice creation.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Buyer from Customer A requesting order list receives only Customer A's orders.\",\n     \"1: Buyer from Customer A modifying an order ID in URL/API to access Customer B's order is denied (not merely hidden in UI).\",\n     \"2: Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A.\",\n     \"3: Changing Price List A later does not alter the price shown/charged on Customer A's already-placed orders.\",\n     \"4: Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day shows next working day as earliest delivery date.\",\n     \"5: Order submitted at/after 14:00 shows the following working day as earliest delivery date.\",\n     \"6: Cancelling a Received order changes its status to Cancelled.\",\n     \"7: Attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked with an appropriate message.\",\n     \"8: When an order's status is successfully saved as Delivered, an invoice is automatically created for it without manual staff action.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"73-suggested-delivery-phases\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a planning/sequencing structure, not itself a functional behaviour — included for completeness only.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Feature delivery is organized into 8 phases (Foundation, Catalogue, Ordering, Staff Ops, Invoicing, Administration, Integrations/Reporting, QA/Production) guiding build order, not end-user-observable behaviour.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 3,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"39-reporting\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Revenue = sum of order value for orders in range, excluding cancelled orders (exact calc rule open).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff select a date range and view 'Orders per Day' report showing date, order count, and order value per day.\",\n     \"1: Staff view 'Top Products' report showing product, quantity sold, revenue, sorted by revenue or quantity.\",\n     \"2: Staff view 'Revenue per Customer' report showing customer, number of orders, revenue.\",\n     \"3: Cancelled orders are excluded from order count/value and revenue totals in all three reports.\",\n     \"4: Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users get 403/404.\",\n     \"5: No orders in selected range produces an empty report (see Empty States) rather than an error.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"40-report-filters\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Only start/end date filtering is implemented in this phase; customer/product/category filters are not built.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff set start date and end date and reports recalculate for that window.\",\n     \"1: If start date is after end date, submission is rejected with a validation message and no report is generated.\",\n     \"2: Date filters apply identically across all three report types and their exports.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"41-report-export\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"CSV export mirrors exactly the columns/rows currently displayed on screen for the active filter.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Staff click 'Download CSV' on a report and receive a file containing the same rows/columns as shown on screen.\",\n     \"1: Only users with report-view permission can trigger the CSV download; unauthorized requests are rejected.\",\n     \"2: If report generation fails, export shows a user-friendly error instead of a broken/empty file.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"42-audit-history\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Audit entries are created automatically and are append-only (no edit/delete via UI).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each listed event (user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed) writes an audit log entry with actor, timestamp, action, and target entity.\",\n     \"1: Only admin users can view the Audit History screen; other roles cannot.\",\n     \"2: Audit log entries cannot be edited or deleted through the application.\",\n     \"3: If writing an audit entry fails, the underlying business action still completes (audit failure does not block the action) and the failure is logged separately.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"43-notifications\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Email send failures are logged but do not block/rollback the underlying action (order confirmation, invite, etc.).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Inviting a user sends an invitation email containing an acceptance link.\",\n     \"1: A password reset request sends an email with a reset link.\",\n     \"2: Confirming an order sends the customer an order-confirmation email; amending sends an amendment email; marking out-for-delivery sends a dispatch email; cancelling/rejecting sends a cancellation email where applicable.\",\n     \"3: If the recipient email is missing/invalid, the notification is skipped and an error is recorded, without blocking the triggering action.\",\n     \"4: If the email provider is unreachable, the send is retried/queued or logged as failed rather than crashing the request.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"44-email-provider\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Only admins can see/configure provider credentials; the app sends via whatever provider is configured.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Provider credentials/configuration (sender address, auth, etc.) are stored securely and not exposed in UI responses to non-admins.\",\n     \"1: Authentication failure with the provider is logged and surfaced on an admin-visible status area rather than silently failing.\",\n     \"2: Only admin can view/edit email provider configuration.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"45-erp-stock-integration\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Nightly CSV import updates StockItem records; portal never calls back to ERP.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A scheduled nightly job reads the ERP-supplied CSV and updates stock quantities for matching products.\",\n     \"1: The portal never writes stock data or inventory transactions back to the ERP (no outbound write calls exist).\",\n     \"2: If the file is missing or malformed, the import fails, previous stock values are left unchanged, and the failure is recorded (visible on System/Import Status screen).\",\n     \"3: Successful imports immediately update stock visibility for customers and staff on catalogue/product pages.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"46-data-retention\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Order/invoice records are never hard-deleted; access is controlled by role, not by data existing only for owner.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Orders and invoices remain stored and queryable for at least 7 years from creation.\",\n     \"1: Deactivating or deleting a user leaves that user's historical orders/invoices intact and viewable by authorized staff/admin and the owning customer's remaining users.\",\n     \"2: Historical records are visible according to the viewer's role/customer scope, same as live records.\",\n     \"3: No UI/API path exists to permanently delete order or invoice records.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"47-responsive-design\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All required screens (customer, staff, admin) must render usably at mobile widths, not just buyer screens.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All pages render usable, functional layouts at common phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths.\",\n     \"1: Buyer-facing flows (catalogue, basket, checkout) are optimized first for mobile usability.\",\n     \"2: No page requires horizontal scrolling or has inaccessible controls at minimum supported mobile width.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"48-performance\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"No numeric SLA is enforced in this phase; system must simply handle stated scale without errors/timeouts.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: System operates correctly under ~300 buyers, ~15 staff, and up to 150 orders/day without errors or timeouts.\",\n     \"1: Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under that load.\",\n     \"2: Under peak load, requests degrade gracefully (e.g., loading indicators, no crashes) rather than failing outright.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"49-security\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Standard controls are baseline requirements applied across all endpoints, not feature-specific.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Passwords are stored hashed (never plaintext) and authentication uses secure, httpOnly/secure session cookies.\",\n     \"1: Every protected endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side regardless of UI state.\",\n     \"2: Unauthenticated/unauthorized API calls return 401/403 without leaking data.\",\n     \"3: All inputs (forms and API payloads) are validated/sanitized; file uploads are checked for type/size before acceptance.\",\n     \"4: Production traffic is served only over HTTPS; HTTP requests are redirected or rejected.\",\n     \"5: Password-reset tokens are single-use