age and prevents the submission.\",\n     \"3: Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all surface user-friendly messages appropriate to the user's role.\",\n     \"4: Session expiration redirects the user to sign-in with an explanatory message rather than a silent failure or raw error.\",\n     \"5: No raw stack traces, SQL errors, or internal technical details are ever rendered to end users in any scenario.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"53-empty-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed scenario gets a distinct, friendly empty-state message/illustration rather than a blank or broken screen.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Search with no matches shows a 'no results' empty state with guidance (e.g., adjust search).\",\n     \"1: An empty basket shows an 'empty basket' state instead of a blank table.\",\n     \"2: No orders/invoices/templates/matching products/report results each show a corresponding tailored empty-state message.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"54-loading-states\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Loading indicators also disable repeat-submission for actions like order submission/checkout to prevent duplicates.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each show a visible loading indicator while the operation is in progress.\",\n     \"1: During order submission or checkout processing, the submit control is disabled/hidden to prevent duplicate submissions while loading.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These screens form the customer-portal navigation; unauthenticated users can only reach sign-in/forgot/reset password, all others require login.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All 16 listed customer screens (sign in, forgot/reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list/detail, saved templates, account/company details, delivery addresses) exist and are navigable.\",\n     \"1: Only sign-in, forgot-password, and reset-password are accessible without authentication; all other customer screens require a logged-in customer session.\",\n     \"2: Attempting to access an authenticated customer screen while logged out redirects to sign-in.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff sign-in is a separate login flow/route from customer sign-in.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All 11 listed staff screens exist (staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list/detail/orders/invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management).\",\n     \"1: Only authenticated staff/admin users can access staff screens; customer users attempting access are denied (403/redirect).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Admin screens require an admin role distinct from general staff role; audit history is read-only.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: All 13 listed admin screens exist (dashboard, users, customers, products, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, import status, audit history, etc.).\",\n     \"1: Only admin-role users can access admin screens; staff without admin rights are denied.\",\n     \"2: Audit history screen is view-only, no edit/delete controls present.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff cancellation/rejection can occur at more stages than pure customer cancellation (business-rule-driven), beyond just Received.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: New orders are created with status Received and progress through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence.\",\n     \"1: Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled.\",\n     \"2: Staff can confirm, edit, reject, or cancel orders per business rules, including at stages beyond Received.\",\n     \"3: Invalid status transitions (e.g., Delivered back to Picking, or customer cancelling a Confirmed order) are rejected with an explanatory message.\",\n     \"4: Reaching Delivered status automatically creates an invoice for the order.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Overdue status is set automatically by a scheduled job once a configured due period elapses while invoice remains Unpaid.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Invoice is created automatically with status Unpaid when its order is marked Delivered.\",\n     \"1: Staff can mark an Unpaid invoice as Paid.\",\n     \"2: A scheduled job transitions Unpaid invoices past their due date to Overdue status automatically.\",\n     \"3: Attempting to mark an already-Paid invoice as Paid again is a no-op or rejected with a message.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treated as conceptual data model support rather than direct user-facing behaviour; main observable effect is that each described business object persists and relates correctly.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each business concept (orders, invoices, baskets, price lists, stock, users, audit logs, email notifications, etc.) is persisted with enough structure to support all behaviours described in the other spans.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"API behaviour is already covered by the corresponding feature spans; this entry just confirms endpoints exist with consistent auth enforcement.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Each listed API area (auth, catalogue, basket, checkout, orders, invoices, administration, reports) exposes endpoints implementing the corresponding behaviours described elsewhere.\",\n     \"1: Every API endpoint enforces the same role/customer-scoping rules as its corresponding UI screen.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Invoice generation is triggered synchronously on the Delivered status change (per acceptance criteria in span 72); other jobs (import, overdue updates, token/invite cleanup, email sending) run on a schedule/queue.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Nightly ERP stock import job runs on schedule automatically without manual trigger.\",\n     \"1: Emails are sent via an asynchronous queue so user-facing requests are not blocked by email sending.\",\n     \"2: Invoice overdue-status update runs periodically and updates all qualifying Unpaid invoices to Overdue.\",\n     \"3: Expired password-reset tokens are periodically cleaned up and become unusable; tokens are also rejected on use after expiry regardless of cleanup timing.\",\n     \"4: Expired/unused invitations are cleaned up or marked expired after their validity window and cannot be accepted afterward.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Storage must support retrieval scoped by permission (e.g., invoice PDFs only by the owning customer or staff).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Product images are stored and served on catalogue/product detail pages.\",\n     \"1: Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for download by the owning customer and authorized staff.\",\n     \"2: ERP CSV files received are retained in storage for later reference/debugging.\",\n     \"3: Stored files are only accessible to users with appropriate permission (e.g., a customer cannot fetch another customer's invoice PDF by guessing a URL).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"PDF is generated once per invoice (on creation) and reused for subsequent downloads rather than regenerated each time.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When an invoice is created, a PDF is generated containing at minimum line