e another company's data (ties to span 50).\",\n     \"1: Product price shown to a customer always derives from that customer's assigned price list.\",\n     \"2: Orders submitted before 14:00 get next working day as earliest delivery; at/after 14:00 get the following working day.\",\n     \"3: Customers can repeat a previous order and can save/name basket templates.\",\n     \"4: Customers can only cancel orders before confirmation; staff can edit orders before confirmation.\",\n     \"5: Online payment, native apps, route planning, and returns/credit notes are not available anywhere in the system.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Out-of-scope items have no corresponding UI/API surface at all in this phase, rather than being present but disabled.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: No UI entry points or API endpoints exist for online card payment, native app-specific APIs, multi-language switching, route optimization, returns, or credit notes.\",\n     \"1: No functionality exists for writing inventory transactions back to the ERP.\",\n     \"2: Advanced pricing features (promotions, coupons, volume/tiered/contract pricing) are absent unless separately approved.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are unresolved clarification items with no concrete behaviour defined yet; defaults/assumptions used elsewhere in this analysis stand until clarified.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: No committed behaviour is implemented purely from this section; items are tracked as open questions pending stakeholder answers, with assumptions noted in the relevant spans above.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"At minimum local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments exist with increasing access restriction toward production.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Separate local, development/test, staging/UAT, and production environments are configured for the application.\",\n     \"1: Production environment enforces HTTPS and restricted access per security requirements (span 49).\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Testing requirements imply the underlying behaviours (already specified in prior spans) must be verifiable via automated/manual tests; listed here as confirmation that each described behaviour has corresponding test coverage.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Automated/manual tests exist exercising successful and failed login, lockout, password reset, invitation, and deactivated-account scenarios.\",\n     \"1: Tests verify customer/staff/admin authorization boundaries and reject unauthorized API access.\",\n     \"2: Tests cover catalogue/search/pricing/stock scenarios including retired products, out-of-stock items, and low-stock status.\",\n     \"3: Tests cover basket/checkout flows including duplicate-submission prevention and delivery-date rules.\",\n     \"4: Tests cover order status transitions, email notification triggers, invoice auto-creation, PDF generation, and payment-status changes.\",\n     \"5: Tests cover report date filtering, total correctness, and CSV export content.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria-examples\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Taken as literal, binding acceptance tests for the described scenarios.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: A buyer from Customer A requesting orders only ever receives Customer A's orders, including when tampering with IDs in the URL/API (returns no data / error for other customers).\",\n     \"1: Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A; if that price list changes later, previously placed orders still show their original price.\",\n     \"2: An order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date; submitted at/after 14:00 gets the following working day.\",\n  